<PublicLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Panda"
  description="How Panda collects, uses, and protects your data. Kenya DPA 2019 compliant."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 md:px-6 md:py-16 prose prose-stone">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-rich-earth/60">
      Version <strong>{version}</strong> &middot; Last updated {lastUpdated}
    </p>

    <div class="rounded-md border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-4 text-sm text-amber-900 not-prose mb-8">
      <strong>Draft pending Kenyan legal review.</strong>
      This Policy is in effect for the pilot launch in Meru and Kirinyaga
      counties. The text will be re-versioned (and you will be asked to
      re-accept) once it has been reviewed by Kenyan legal counsel and Panda
      has been registered with the Office of the Data Protection Commissioner
      (ODPC) under §18 of the Data Protection Act 2019.
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who we are &amp; the law that applies</h2>
    <p>
      Panda is a horticulture planning and logging tool operated by
      <strong>Upstate Web Co.</strong>, acting in Kenya under its sister-brand
      <strong>Shira</strong>. We are the data controller for personal data
      processed through Panda. This Policy describes the personal data we
      collect, why we collect it, how we share it, how long we keep it, and
      the rights you have under the
      <strong>Kenya Data Protection Act 2019</strong> ("DPA 2019"). If any
      part of this Policy conflicts with a non-waivable right you have under
      that Act, the Act prevails.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account data</strong> — your name, email, phone (optional), county, sub-county, farm name. Required to operate your account.</li>
      <li><strong>Farm records</strong> — crop, season, acreage, planting / harvest dates, costs, yields, supplier and buyer names. These are your records; we host them so you can access them across devices.</li>
      <li><strong>Disease detection</strong> — photographs you upload, the model's diagnosis, your opt-in flag for training. Photographs are stored on Cloudflare R2.</li>
      <li><strong>Technical data</strong> — IP address, browser / device, language, timezone, when you logged in, when you accepted these policies. Captured for security and for the DPA 2019 §30 burden of proof on consent.</li>
      <li><strong>Communications</strong> — messages you send to support, including attachments.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Lawful basis (DPA 2019 §30)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Performance of a contract.</strong> Account and farm-record processing is necessary to deliver the service you signed up for.</li>
      <li><strong>Consent.</strong> Disease-photo training, marketing email, and analytics cookies (when introduced) rely on your specific opt-in. You can withdraw at any time.</li>
      <li><strong>Legal obligation.</strong> Tax-relevant records (cost and revenue entries) are retained for the period required by the Income Tax Act §23 (currently five years).</li>
      <li><strong>Legitimate interest.</strong> Fraud prevention, error logging, and aggregate analytics for product improvement, balanced against your rights.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. How we share data</h2>
    <p>We do not sell your data. We share with the following processors, each only to the extent strictly necessary:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Hetzner Online GmbH</strong> (Germany) — primary hosting for the API and database.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> (USA / global edge) — DNS, edge caching, R2 object storage for disease photographs.</li>
      <li><strong>Resend, Inc.</strong> (USA) — transactional email (verification, password reset, receipts).</li>
      <li><strong>Sentry</strong> (USA) — error monitoring; we do not send identifiable personal data to Sentry, only error stack traces and an opaque user identifier.</li>
      <li><strong>Plant disease AI provider (planned, not yet active)</strong> — once activated, photographs flagged for training will be sent to a third-party plant-pathology model provider. We will re-version this Policy and re-prompt for consent before any data leaves Panda for this purpose.</li>
      <li><strong>Mobile-money providers</strong> — when paid tiers launch, transactional data will pass through Safaricom Daraja for M-Pesa. Safaricom's own privacy notice applies to that processing.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Cross-border transfers (DPA 2019 §49)</h2>
    <p>
      Hetzner stores your data primarily in Germany (EU); Cloudflare's edge
      network and Resend operate from multiple jurisdictions including the
      USA. Where data is transferred outside Kenya, we rely on adequacy
      regimes (EU GDPR) or contractual safeguards. You may request the
      specific safeguards in place by writing to
      <a href="mailto:dpo@shira.farm">dpo@shira.farm</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Retention</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Account &amp; farm records: while your account is active, plus 5 years for tax-relevant records.</li>
      <li>Disease photographs: 30 days after deletion request; opted-in photographs retained while opt-in remains in force.</li>
      <li>Server logs (IP, request paths): 30 days.</li>
      <li>Backup snapshots: 30 days rolling.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Your rights (DPA 2019 §§26–35)</h2>
    <p>You have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>access the personal data we hold about you;</li>
      <li>request correction of inaccurate data;</li>
      <li>request deletion of your data (subject to legal-retention exceptions);</li>
      <li>object to processing based on legitimate interest;</li>
      <li>withdraw consent (e.g. for disease-photo training) at any time;</li>
      <li>data portability (export your records in a structured format);</li>
      <li>lodge a complaint with the Office of the Data Protection Commissioner.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these rights, write to
      <a href="mailto:dpo@shira.farm">dpo@shira.farm</a>. We will respond
      within 30 days (DPA 2019 §29).
    </p>

    <h2>8. Complaints &amp; the regulator</h2>
    <p>
      If you are not satisfied with our handling of your data, you may
      complain to the Office of the Data Protection Commissioner:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Office of the Data Protection Commissioner</strong></li>
      <li>P.O. Box 30920–00100, Nairobi, Kenya</li>
      <li>Phone: +254 20 4900800</li>
      <li>Email: <a href="mailto:info@odpc.go.ke">info@odpc.go.ke</a></li>
      <li>Website: <a href="https://www.odpc.go.ke">odpc.go.ke</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Breach notification (DPA 2019 §43)</h2>
    <p>
      If we discover a personal-data breach likely to result in risk to you,
      we will notify the ODPC within 72 hours of becoming aware of it, and
      notify affected users without undue delay where high risk is involved.
      Suspected breaches: <a href="mailto:security@shira.farm">security@shira.farm</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Children</h2>
    <p>
      Panda is not directed at users under 18. We do not knowingly collect
      data from children. If you believe a child has provided personal data,
      contact us and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We re-version this Policy when our practices or the law change. The
      version above is canonical; the application will prompt you to re-accept
      the updated Policy before continuing if the version changes.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Contact</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Data Protection Officer: <a href="mailto:dpo@shira.farm">dpo@shira.farm</a></li>
      <li>Security incidents: <a href="mailto:security@shira.farm">security@shira.farm</a></li>
      <li>General: <a href="mailto:support@shira.farm">support@shira.farm</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</PublicLayout>
